{"title":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","category":"Engineering","bank":"nta_abhyas_jee_main","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Properties of Triangles","count":5,"questions":[{"id":91688,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Properties of Triangles","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"Suppose that the side lengths of a triangle are three consecutive integers and one of the angles is twice another. The number of such triangles is/are","options":["<math> <mn>1</mn> </math>","<math> <mn>0</mn></math>","<math> <mn>4</mn></math>","<math> <mn>2</mn></math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"Let <math> <mtext>B</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>A</mtext> </math> and <math> <mtext>B</mtext><mtext>D</mtext> </math> be the bisector of angle <math> <mrow> <mtext>B</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> then<br /><br /><math><mrow><mtext>CD</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>ab</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo> & </mo> <mtext>AD</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>bc</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Now,  <math> <mrow> <mo>Δ</mo> <mtext>ABC</mtext> <mo> and </mo> <mo>Δ</mo> <mtext>BDC</mtext> </mrow> </math> are similar, so<br /><br /><math><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mtext>BC</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>AC</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>CD</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>BC</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>⇒</mo> <msup> <mtext>a</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>ab</mtext> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>b</mtext> <mo> ⇒ </mo> <msup> <mtext>b</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>a</mtext> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math> ......(i)<br /><br />Since, <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>></mo><mtext>a</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo></mrow> </math> Either <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </math> or <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo> </math> if <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo> </math> then [From Eq.(i)]<br /><br /><math><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"><mrow><mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mtext>a</mtext> <mo>⇒</mo> <mtext>c</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math><br /><br /> <img alt=\"\" src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fnta_abhyas%252Fjee_main%252Fimages%252Ffvvvvvv.JPG%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fnta_abhyas%2Fjee_main%2Fimages%2Ffvvvvvv.JPG?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fnta_abhyas%2Fjee_main%2Fimages%2Ffvvvvvv.JPG?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 169px;\" /><br /><math><mtext>c</mtext> </math> is integer <math><mrow><mo>⇒</mo></mrow></math> <math> <mrow><mtext>a</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>c</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow> </math> but then, no triangle will form.<br />If <math> <mrow> <mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> then obviously <math> <mrow> <mtext>c</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow> </math> and then, [from Eq. (i)]<br /><br /><math> <msup> <mfenced> <mrow> <mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </mfenced> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>=</mo><mtext>a</mtext><mfenced> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mtext>a</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </mfenced> </math><br /><br /><math> <mo>⇒</mo><msup> <mtext>a</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>or</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>a</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn> </math><br /><br /><math> <mo>∴</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>a</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mtext>b</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>c</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn> </math> is the only possible solution.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main) 2020","_marksId":"6151e863ae42edeea77c0910"},{"id":91689,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Properties of Triangles","exam":"Engineering","examName":"NTA Abhyas (JEE Main)","q":"The inradius of the triangle having sides <math><mn>26, 28, 30</mn></math> units is","options":[],"answer":"8","solution":"<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>26</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>42</mn></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>42</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>42</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>26</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>42</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>28</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|